/P 158 0 R
/E (Natural gas is a naturally occurring fossil fuel found deep beneath the Earth's surface, often alongside crude oil. It mainly consists of methane and is widely used as an important source of energy across the world. It plays a significant role in electricity generation, transportation, household cooking and industrial production. Natural gas is considered a cleaner-burning fossil fuel compared to coal and petroleum because it releases fewer harmful pollutants and less carbon dioxide when burned. In India, its importance is increasing due to growing energy requirements, industrial development and the need for more sustainable energy sources. Companies like Oil and Natural Gas Corporation \(ONGC\) play an important role in exploring and producing natural gas, helping meet the country's domestic energy demand and reducing dependence on imports)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
